// Structure navigation marks, including COMPOSITE (multi-word) forms parsed from
// bare tokens: `to coda`, `ds al coda`, `dc al fine`. Segno/Coda targets and
// "To Coda" sit above; the jump-FROM instructions ("D.S. al Coda", "D.C. al
// Fine", "Fine") sit below the staff, right-aligned at the barline (Gould,
// Behind Bars). A mark is an event at a MOMENT, and `|` takes no time: written
// before the bar (`… c' to coda |`) or after it (`… g1 | ds al coda`) it stands at
// the same barline — a text to the bar's left, a sign to its right — so both
// spellings are exercised here and the one after the LAST bar is drawn too.
// LILYPOND-REF: lily/mark-engraver.cc; scm/output-lib.scm.
title "Navigation marks"
time 4/4

part rh { clef treble }

section Main {
  rh {
    segno g4 a b c' |
    g4 a b c' to coda |
    g1 | ds al coda
    coda g4 a b c' |
    g1 dc al fine |
    g1 | fine
  }
}

form main { Main }

score main "navigation-marks" { staff rh }
